# What the Docker build does not need (owner, 2026-10-21: "napravi da pokrecem lokalno iz dockera").
#
# The build context is what Docker copies into the image, and this working copy is 2.6 GB: two
# gigabytes of it are recorded match replays, 283 MB is the build output of the last local build,
# and the rest is the IDE and the node modules. Sending all of that to the daemon on every build
# is minutes of nothing.
#
# **.git is NOT excluded, and that is deliberate.** The build writes the commit into the jar so the
# Settings page can say which code is running (the version, owner, 2026-10-21). Without the
# repository in the build stage there is no commit to write, and the jar would answer "unknown" for
# the one thing it is there to answer.

# The build output of a local build, and the dependencies of a local build.
target/
node_modules/

# The recorded match replays: runtime data, two gigabytes of it, regenerated by the app.
replay-data/

# The local PostgreSQL's dumps and the working documents - the owner's own notes, not source.
backups/
*.md
*.pdf

# The IDE and the editor's leftovers.
.idea/
.vscode/
.settings/
*.iml

# The generated replay of the proposal match viewer (58 MB), written by the app at runtime.
src/main/resources/static/demo/service/ui/proposal/match.json
src/main/resources/static/demo/service/ui/match.json

.DS_Store
